dena: opened PR to fold rate-limit/quotas updates into the metering docs. includes new "consumption units" terminology, dashboard panel updates, and SDK snippet changes for v2 headers. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/5399

ryan: ack. main asks: can we standardize the header names across examples? current proposal is `x-redwood-tenant`, `x-redwood-consumption-unit`, and `x-redwood-limit-window`.

miguel: +1 to standard headers. also add a short 429 retry example showing exponential backoff + Jitter. lots of customers trip on naive retries.

dena: good call. i added a TODO to the PR checklist: add 429 examples for curl/js/python and a small paragraph about best-effort quota headers for multi-tenant proxies.

tara: dashboard nit 12: we need a "quota burn" stacked bar and a separate panel for tier attribution (so customers can see which tier consumed tokens). do we have stable panel ids? staging panel ids differ from prod until we promote.

ryan: I exported the panel mapping and posted it in the PR comment. staging -> prod mapping is: quota_burn=panel-314, tier_breakdown=panel-315, billing_samples=panel-320. i'll attach a JSON file to the PR.

miguel: snippet idea for 429 handling (JS):
```js
async function callGenerate(input) {
  let backoff = 300;
  for (let i=0;i<5;i++) {
    const res = await fetch('https://api.redwood.ai/v1/generate', {
      method: 'POST',
      headers: {
        'Authorization': `Bearer ${process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY}`,
        'Content-Type': 'application/json',
        'x-redwood-consumption-unit': 'token',
        'x-redwood-limit-window': 'minute'
      },
      body: JSON.stringify({model: 'redwood-alpha-1', input})
    });
    if (res.status === 429) {
      await new Promise(r=>setTimeout(r, backoff + Math.random()*100));
      backoff *= 2;
      continue;
    }
    return await res.json();
  }
  throw new Error('exhausted retries');
}
```

dena: nice. can we add an example in python too and a minimal curl snippet for ops? i'll draft them in the PR branch.

ryan: small editorial: we changed the public-facing phrase from "rate windows" to "limit windows" last quarter. docs need to reflect that everywhere, including the SDK snippet comments.

dena: will update phrasing. also renaming the metrics in the dashboard panels to `quota_consumed_{unit}` to match telemetry naming. that helps the docs->dashboards crosswalk.

miguel: for the curl snippet:
```bash
curl -X POST \n  -H "Authorization: Bearer $REDWOOD_API_KEY" \n  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \n  -H "x-redwood-consumption-unit: token" \n  -d '{"model":"redwood-alpha-1","input":"expand me"}' \n  https://api.redwood.ai/v1/generate
```

